# SHACL shapes for the 2Wiki Biography/Work Ontology.
#
# GENERATED FILE -- do not hand-edit. Regenerate with:
#     python ontology/generate_shacl_shapes.py
# after any change to ontology.ttl.
#
# Design notes
# ------------
# * One sh:NodeShape per declared property, targeted with sh:targetSubjectsOf
#   so it fires on real assertions (including ones inferred by RDFS
#   subPropertyOf entailment, since run_agent_pipeline.py validates with
#   pyshacl inference="rdfs").
# * Deliberately NO sh:class check against a property's own rdfs:domain/range.
#   run_agent_pipeline.py always validates with inference="rdfs" and passes
#   ontology.ttl (which carries those very rdfs:domain/rdfs:range triples) as
#   ont_graph. RDFS entailment (rules rdfs2/rdfs3) means any subject/object of
#   a property is automatically inferred to have that property's declared
#   domain/range type *regardless of what was actually asserted* -- so an
#   sh:class shape tied to the same class would always pass, catching nothing.
#   Verified empirically: an Organization wrongly given ex:hasDeathDate, and
#   ex:hasSpouse wrongly pointing at a Country, both validate as conformant
#   under inference="rdfs" despite being real domain/range violations, and
#   both correctly fail under inference=None. Domain/range compatibility is
#   instead enforced directly in kg_builder_agent.py._validate_extractions
#   before any Turtle is written, so no coverage gap results from omitting it
#   here -- but a hand-added sh:class shape here would be misleading, since it
#   would look like a live check while doing nothing under how this project
#   actually invokes pyshacl.
# * sh:nodeKind (sh:IRI / sh:Literal) is unaffected by that entailment and
#   still catches a value of the wrong RDF term kind for a property.
# * sh:datatype / sh:or (datatype properties) is likewise unaffected and
#   still catches malformed or wrongly-typed literals.
# * sh:maxCount 1 is used only for project properties judged genuinely
#   single-valued. hasCountryOfOrigin is intentionally not restricted: films,
#   organizations, and other artifacts may legitimately originate in multiple
#   countries. Cardinality must never force a repair agent to delete supported
#   source facts merely to obtain SHACL conformance. No property in ontology.ttl
#   is currently declared owl:FunctionalProperty, so these constraints are
#   explicit project-level decisions rather than ontology-derived axioms.
# * This is intentionally an *open* shapes file (no sh:closed): kg_builder_agent.py
#   already rejects unknown attributes/predicates and domain/range mismatches
#   in Python before any Turtle is written, so SHACL's job here is to catch what
#   that layer doesn't -- cardinality, literal datatype well-formedness, and a
#   second independent check on object-property value types.

@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/2wiki-ontology#> .
@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# 0. GENERIC ENTITY SHAPE
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every individual kg_builder_agent produces is typed with owl:NamedIndividual
# alongside its domain class (see kg_builder_agent._add_entity). This is a
# lightweight sanity check that survives even hand-edited or reasoner-derived
# graphs: every named individual must carry at least one rdf:type from this
# ontology's own class hierarchy.
ex:NamedIndividualShape
    a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass owl:NamedIndividual ;
    sh:property [
        sh:path rdf:type ;
        sh:minCount 1 ;
        sh:message "owl:NamedIndividual must also have at least one rdf:type from the ontology's class hierarchy" ;
    ] .

